## 7.4 Quick recap

### Purpose

Give the user a short overview of their running progress.

### Known metrics

1. Highest score.
2. First run or period.
3. Latest run or period.

### Highest score

Displays the highest recorded score and the date on which it occurred.

### First run

Displays the score associated with the earliest run or period.

### Latest run

Displays the score associated with the most recent run or period.

### Time grouping behavior

The recap changes based on the selected time grouping.

| Grouping | First and latest values represent |
|---|---|
| Daily | Individual runs |
| Weekly | Weekly average scores |
| Monthly | Monthly average scores |
| Quarterly | Quarterly average scores |
| Yearly | Yearly average scores |

### Visual hierarchy

The numerical score should be prominent.

Supporting labels and dates should have lower visual emphasis.

Anton is used for large metric values.

**Not yet verified:** Exact card arrangement, component dimensions, internal padding, metric typography sizes, and whether the three metrics are separate cards or one grouped container.

