## 7.5 Performance chart

### Purpose

Visualize running performance over time.

### Chart modes

- Score.
- Volume.

### Score mode

Displays average running score across the selected time grouping.

### Volume mode

Displays running distance across the selected time grouping.

### Chart controls

The chart has a control to switch between Score and Volume.

### Chart interaction

The user can:

- Select a chart point.
- View the corresponding period.
- See a vertical selection indicator.
- Update the metrics displayed above the chart.
- Drag horizontally to navigate historical data.

### Score chart behavior

Periods without eligible scores are skipped.

The chart connects available data points across the missing periods.

### Volume chart behavior

Periods without runs display zero distance.

### Chart layout

The chart uses time on the horizontal axis and the selected metric on the vertical axis.

Approximately 12 points should be visible on a mobile screen.

**Not yet verified:** Exact chart dimensions, gridline visibility, stroke width, point radius, axis typography, selected-point colors, and tooltip styling.

