# 11. ADD RUN SCREEN

## 11.1 Purpose

Allow the user to manually record a running activity.

## 11.2 Fields

The known field structure is:

1. Title.
2. Description.
3. Location.
4. Date.
5. Time.
6. Distance.
7. Duration.
8. Pace.
9. Average heart rate.
10. Elevation gain.
11. Cadence.

### Title

Required.

Defaults to "Outdoor run".

### Description

Optional text input.

### Location

Optional text input.

### Date

Required date input.

### Time

Required time input.

### Distance

Required numeric input.

Unit: kilometers.

### Duration

Required duration input.

### Pace

Required and calculated from distance and duration.

### Average heart rate

Required numeric input.

Unit: beats per minute.

### Elevation gain

Optional numeric input.

Unit: meters.

### Cadence

Optional numeric input.

Unit: steps per minute.

## 11.3 Interdependent fields

Distance, duration, and pace are synchronized.

- Changing distance recalculates pace.
- Changing duration recalculates pace.
- Changing pace recalculates distance.
- Duration remains unchanged when pace is edited.

## 11.4 Actions

Save the run.

Return or navigate back.

## 11.5 Validation

Required fields must be completed.

Invalid values should display an error on the corresponding field.

Overlapping runs must be blocked before saving.

**Not yet verified:** Exact input component variants, field spacing, field grouping, helper text, error state, and button placement.

